#!/usr/bin/env bash
# fusion-turn-budget — the orchestrator's Phase-2 Turn budget, resolved from
# configuration. Read once at Setup (agents/orchestrator.md Setup Step 2,
# skills/setup/SKILL.md Step 2) instead of the number being written into the
# prompt.
#
# Usage:
#   fusion-turn-budget
#
# Output on stdout, one KEY=value line:
#
#   max_turns=5
#
# Every diagnostic the configuration loader returned goes to stderr, one line
# each, whatever its class. A dropped key is one class (the line names the key
# and why, and the budget falls through to the default); the costliest line is
# not a drop at all: a leftover fusion-guard.json at the project root, which
# fusion no longer reads a byte of, is named on every call until it is deleted,
# and no key was dropped because the file was never read. Nothing narrows the
# stream to drops, and nothing should — a loop that printed only drops would
# silence exactly that line. This is the one call that reads the budget, so it
# is where the loader's advice is heard.
#
# Exit codes:
#   0  resolved.
#   1  usage error.
#   2  no fusion workbench above the working directory, so there is no project
#      layer to merge and a project that declared its own budget would be told
#      the plugin's. No budget is printed; the caller reports it unresolved.
#   3  the plugin's compiled hooks are missing, so nothing could be asked. Its
#      own code and not 2: "this project configures no budget" is an answer
#      about the project, and a broken install must never be reported as one.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Why the budget is read rather than stated
#
# It was stated: `5`, in seven places in agents/orchestrator.md, in four
# spellings, one of which already called it a "default" while no source could
# override it (issue 260811-1712_*_max-turns-is-hardcoded-in-eight-places-and-cannot-be-set-per-project.md). Seven copies of one fact go stale together
# and no project could change any of them.
#
# The value now lives in hooks/lib/config.ts DEFAULTS — once — and is overridden
# per project through the file that already exists for per-project settings:
#
#   fusion.json   {"orchestrator": {"maxTurns": 12}}
#
# merged per leaf over the defaults. Two layers, that file and DEFAULTS, and
# nothing between them: the plugin-level layer existed for the guard settings a
# project could narrow, and went with them on 2026-08-16. A project whose root
# still carries the earlier fusion-guard.json is told so on every guarded tool
# call, because a budget left in that file is not read.
#
# The work is hooks/dist/turn-budget.js, resolved relative to this script rather
# than through $FUSION_PLUGIN_ROOT, so an install copy and a work tree each run
# their own build. node is already a hard requirement — the guard hooks are node
# programs (hooks/hooks.json).

set -euo pipefail

here="$(cd "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")" && pwd)"
entry="$here/../hooks/dist/turn-budget.js"

if [ ! -f "$entry" ]; then
  echo "fusion-turn-budget: $entry is missing — the plugin's compiled hooks are not installed." >&2
  exit 3
fi

exec node "$entry" "$@"
